      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Amlodipine 20 mg once daily is double the usual maximum dose of 10 mg per day. Doses above 10 mg raise the risk of peripheral edema, hypotension, and reflex tachycardia, and they usually add little extra blood pressure control.\n\nWhich of these do you want?\n\n1. **Enter 10 mg by mouth once daily.** This is the standard maximum.\n2. **Enter 20 mg as written.** I'll need you to confirm that the dose is intentional. If you'd like, I can add a note with your rationale, such as \"dose above labeled max, confirmed by attending.\"\n3. **Try a different regimen.** If 10 mg isn't enough, you could add a second agent such as an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide-type diuretic. That choice is yours as the prescriber.\n\nTell me which option you want and I'll enter the order."
      }
     ],
